---
// Damage formula guide: how ATK, defense stats, and DEF Down interact in the damage pipeline
import GuideLayout from '../../../layouts/horizon-walker/GuideLayout.astro';
import {
  ATK_TYPES,
  DEFENSE_MAPPING,
  DEF_EXAMPLES_POSITIVE,
  DEF_EXAMPLES_NEGATIVE,
} from '../../../data/horizon-walker/combat-mechanics.js';
import '../../../styles/games/horizon-walker/hw-combat-mechanics.css';

const breadcrumbs = [{ name: 'Damage Formula' }];
---

<GuideLayout
  title="Horizon Walker Damage Formula and Defense Guide"
  description="How Horizon Walker calculates damage: the ATK and defense formula, which defense stat each damage type uses, and how DEF Down including negative DEF amplifies your damage."
  pageTitle="Damage Formula and Defense"
  subtitle="How the game turns your ATK into damage, which defense stat actually gets checked, and why DEF Down is the strongest debuff in the game."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <section class="hw-guide-section" id="formula">
    <h2 class="hw-section-title">The Core Formula</h2>
    <div class="hw-section-content">
      <p>Every skill hit rolls the following pipeline:</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hw-mech-formula">
      damage = skill% x ATK x defense multiplier x level multiplier x battle ratio
    </div>
    <ul class="hw-guide-list">
      <li><strong>skill%</strong> is the skill's damage coefficient (the percentages on skill pages).</li>
      <li><strong>ATK</strong> is the attacker's stat chosen by the skill type, see below.</li>
      <li><strong>defense multiplier</strong> comes from exactly one defense stat on the target, see below.</li>
      <li><strong>level multiplier</strong> is the level difference rule, see the Level Difference page.</li>
      <li><strong>battle ratio</strong> is a per battle global, normally 1.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="hw-section-content">
      <p>Critical hits, weakness attacks, and buff effects multiply on top of this base.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="hw-guide-section" id="atk">
    <h2 class="hw-section-title">Which ATK Is Used</h2>
    <div class="hw-mech-table-wrap">
      <table class="hw-mech-table" aria-label="Skill type to ATK stat mapping">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Skill Type</th>
            <th scope="col">ATK Stat</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {ATK_TYPES.map(row => (
            <tr>
              <td>{row.skill}</td>
              <td>{row.stat}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="hw-guide-section" id="defense-stat">
    <h2 class="hw-section-title">Which Defense Is Used</h2>
    <div class="hw-section-content">
      <p>
        This is the part most players get wrong. A skill's <strong>elemental property decides the defense
        stat, and it replaces physical defense entirely</strong>. Cora's Heat damage never touches Slash
        DEF: it rolls against the target's FireResist.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="hw-mech-table-wrap">
      <table class="hw-mech-table" aria-label="Damage type to defense stat mapping">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Damage Type</th>
            <th scope="col">Defense Stat Checked</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {DEFENSE_MAPPING.map(row => (
            <tr>
              <td>{row.damage}</td>
              <td>{row.stat}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="hw-info-box">
      <div class="hw-info-box-title">Practical takeaway</div>
      <div class="hw-info-box-content">
        A boss with heavy physical DEF but low elemental Resist takes far more damage from elemental
        attackers. When a wall boss stops you, check which Resist is lowest and bring that element,
        it can be worth more than raw ATK.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="hw-guide-section" id="defense-multiplier">
    <h2 class="hw-section-title">The Defense Multiplier</h2>
    <div class="hw-section-content">
      <p>With the matched defense stat D, the multiplier is 1 - D / (D + 1000):</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hw-mech-table-wrap">
      <table class="hw-mech-table" aria-label="Damage taken by defense value">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Defense</th>
            <th scope="col">Damage Taken</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {DEF_EXAMPLES_POSITIVE.map(row => (
            <tr>
              <td>{row.def}</td>
              <td>{row.taken}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="hw-section-content">
      <p>
        It has diminishing returns: the first 250 defense removes 20% of incoming damage, but going from
        3000 to 9000 only removes another 15%. Defense can never fully nullify damage.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="hw-guide-section" id="negative-def">
    <h2 class="hw-section-title">Negative DEF: The Real Reason DEF Down Is Broken</h2>
    <div class="hw-section-content">
      <p>
        When DEF Down pushes a target's defense <strong>below zero</strong>, the game switches to a
        separate formula: 1 + |DEF| / 1000. That is flat damage amplification with <strong>no cap</strong>:
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="hw-mech-table-wrap">
      <table class="hw-mech-table" aria-label="Damage taken at negative defense values">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Defense</th>
            <th scope="col">Damage Taken</th>
            <th scope="col">Note</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {DEF_EXAMPLES_NEGATIVE.map(row => (
            <tr class="hw-mech-highlight">
              <td>{row.def}</td>
              <td>{row.taken}</td>
              <td>{row.note || ''}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="hw-example-box">
      <div class="hw-example-title">Why Palekar enables one shots</div>
      <div class="hw-example-content">
        Her [Unstable] from Verse of Ordeal cuts All DEF by 1140, up to 1340 with her Evasion scaling.
        On a boss whose defense drops below zero, the whole team hits at 2.14x to 2.34x damage, on top of
        the increased DMG Taken the debuff also applies. That is why DEF Down is a bigger damage amp than
        most attack buffs.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</GuideLayout>
